{{also|Appendix:Variations of "mis"}}

==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|mis-|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=ang}}, from Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*missa-||wrongly, badly}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*mitto||mutual, reciprocal}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*meyt-||to replace, switch, exchange, swap}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|miss-|lang=de}}, {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=de}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=is}}. Compare also {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|més-|lang=fr}}, {{term|mé-||mis-|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|mes-||mis-|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|frk|en}} {{m|frk|*mis-}}, {{m|frk|*missa-||mis-}}, from the same Proto-Germanic source above.

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# [[bad]], [[badly]], [[wrong]], [[wrongly]]
# [[lack]] or [[failure]]

====Derived terms====
* See [[:Category:English words prefixed with mis-]]

====See also====
* [[mal-]]
* [[miso-]]

